      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Clopidogrel is increasingly used as an antiplatelet agent along with aspirin in coronary stenting due to its safety profile and clinical efficacy. This report describes a case of successful direct coronary stenting in a transplanted heart with the use of clopidogrel and aspirin therapy. Vessel patency was preserved with no evidence of in stent restenosis on 4-month follow-up angiography."},
